Subject: ArcHull: cover the polyline's error in the hull margin
Upstream-file: pcbnew/router/pns_utils.cpp (ArcHull)
Why: ArcHull offsets the arc's polyline (ConvertToPolyline(ARC_LOW_DEF),
 error up to 20 um) by the clearance plus a margin of
 SHAPE_ARC::DefaultAccuracyForPCB() (5 um). The polyline is not the arc: its
 chords dip inside the arc on the outer side and its vertices stand outside it
 on the inner side, so the hull comes closer to the arc than the clearance
 wherever that exceeds the margin. A walkaround path that follows the hull then collides
 with the arc it walked around, the walkaround never settles, and a route
 past an arc fails (tests/run_tests.py t_arc_obstacle: 8 um short on the
 synthetic "arc" board). ConvertToPolyline splits its error on either side of
 the arc, so the hull is short by at most half of it: the margin is now
 ARC_LOW_DEF / 2 plus 1 um for integer rounding (an earlier version of this
 patch used the whole ARC_LOW_DEF, twice the need: review r3 P-2).
Upstream: yes - the same code is in KiCad master (2026-10-05); not yet proposed.

--- a/pcbnew/router/pns_utils.cpp
+++ b/pcbnew/router/pns_utils.cpp
@@ -3,6 +3,10 @@
  *
